\par\par \b \uc2  Canada dlr opens at C$1.4788, new intra-day low. \b0\par\par\uc2 704 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juli 1998\par 14:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par FORECAST RANGE   1.4730/1.4800\tab ASIAN CLOSE    1.4757\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par US$ SUPPORT 1.4600  RESISTANCE 1.4830 HIGH 1.4790 LOW 1.4744\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par CANADA OPEN 1.4788 HIGH 1.4790\tab EUROPE OPEN    1.4754\par PREV CLOSE  1.4747 LOW  1.4744\tab HIGH 1.4788 LOW 1.4746\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par FRIDAY, JULY 10\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TREND: BEARISH, ACTIVITY: ACTIVE\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par *Canada's dollar opened at C$1.4788 (US$0.6762), record low\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par intra-day level, as market tested U.S. dollar topside,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par following weak tone in overseas markets. *USD off vs mark on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par optimistic view on Russia, slipped vs yen as well. *CAD hit\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par C$1.4790 (US$0.6761) in Asia overnight, record overseas trading\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par low. *After recovering to around C$1.4740/45 before Canadian\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trading hours, CAD started to weaken on news that Canada's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par employment fell for second consecutive month in June.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par *Employment fell by 35,900 with most declines in farm sector,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par after drop of 7,300 in May. *Economists on average had forecast\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par employment rising 26,000. *Full impact of GM strike seen coming\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in July data.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TORONTO, July 10 (Reuters) - The Canadian dollar opened at C$1.4788 (US$0.6762), a record low intra-day level, as the market tested the U.S. dollar topside, following a weaker tone in overseas markets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "We got up to C$.1.4792 (US$0.6760) earlier, that was the high, and come off since because the dollar/yen's come off," one trader said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The U.S. dollar fell against the mark as the market turned optimistic from Thursday's bearish views of Russia's economic problems. This has pulled the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  down to 140 yen from above 141 yen on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Canadian dollar hit C$1.4790 (US$0.6761) in Asia overnight, a record overseas trading low.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The market was a bit jittery ahead of the 0900 EDT/1300 GMT window of Bank of Canada money market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  this morning.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par After recovering to around C$1.4740/45 (US$0.6784/0.6782) before Canadian trading began at 0800 EDT/1200 GMT, the Canadian unit started to weaken on news that Canada's employment fell for the second consecutive month in June.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Employment fell by 35,900 to 14.24 million in June with most declines in the agricultural sector, after falling by 7,300 in May. Economists on average had forecast employment rising 26,000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Full impact of the General Motors strike is expected to be felt in the July jobs data.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In cross trading, Canada fell to 1.2292 marks from 1.2390 marks at the previous close here, and to 94.84 yen from 95.53 yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Mario Angastiniotis, senior economist at Standard & Poor's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par MMS, said he expected the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to sell\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. dollars around a key psychological level of C$1.4800\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (US$0.6757).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is unlikely to raise its key lending\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rate to lure investors to Canada with a higher return unless\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trading becomes panicky, he predicted.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "As long as there's no momentum behind to push it (the U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  dollar) to higher spot levels (against the Canadian dollar), I\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par think the bank will basically let it ride without doing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par anything on the interest rate front," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Canada's bearish jobs report came on the heels of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thursday's news of weak housing starts for June, which fell for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the third consecutive month, by 4.6 percent. Strikes in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par province of Ontario slowed construction.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     This morning, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market saw little impact of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. producer price index, while U.S. treasuries eased a bit as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the core rate rose a bigger-than-expected 0.2 percent in June.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  The overall PPI showed a benign inflation picture, falling 0.1\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent. Economists had expected the overall PPI to be\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par unchanged after a 0.2-percent rise in May. The core rate,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par excluding food and energy prices, was forecast to show a rise\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of 0.1 percent after a 0.2-percent rise.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     (Masaru Sato, Reuters Toronto newsroom (416) 941-8107,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par toronto.newsroom@reuters.com))\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du7a00z5t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
