\par\par \b \uc2  Canada to swap bond proceeds to US dlrs-dealers. \b0\par\par\uc2 200 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juni 1998\par 20:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, June 22 (Reuters) - Canada will swap proceeds of its planned four billion mark 10-year bond offering into floating-rate U.S. dollars, according to swaps dealers in New York. \par \par \uc2  The floating rate U.S. dollar proceeds will be tied to the six-month London Interbank Offered Rate (LIBOR), according to dealers. \par \par \uc2  Some of the funds may be used to replenish dollar reserves Canada spent defending the Canadian dollar against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the most recent round of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  last Monday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  A part of the swapped funds will be invested in U.S. securities with maturities less than one-year, according to some traders. \par \par \uc2  An official at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Canada declined to say what \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  the end-proceeds would be held in. He only said that proceeds would be used for the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. \par \par \uc2  The issue will be priced off the German bunds curve rather than any one issue, dealers said. Deutsche Bank and Credit Suisse First Boston are lead-managers. \par \par \uc2  (( - Apu Sikri, N.A. Treasury Desk; 212 859-1562)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6m02ecj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
