\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada Intervenes \highlight\uc2  -2: Repeated  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Seen \b0\par\par\uc2 230 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 1998\par 18:50\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market repeatedly early Thursday afternoon to sell U.S. dollars at C$1.4690 and C$1.4695 in an effort to smooth out trading action, said a trader in Toronto. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was at C$1.4692 at 12:43 p.m. EDT (1643 GMT). \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's unofficial policy is to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets after intraday moves in either direction of 70 ticks or more in order to contain volatility. The U.S. dollar closed at C$1.4615 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The bank was first reported \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  at C$1.4685 at around 11:15 a.m EDT (1515 GMT). \par \par \uc2  In cases of sustained pressure against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  will usually \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at each 5-tick level. \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market sources reported seeing a pattern of repeated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday morning after the first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at C$1.4685. \par \par \uc2  The Canadian dollar rebounded Wednesday from its recent weakness after the Bank of Japan and the U.S. Federal Reserve Board engaged in concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the yen. \par \par \uc2  But the recovery did not prove sustainable Thursday morning, and the Canadian dollar has been sliding steadily downward through the session. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires  06-18-98 \par \par \uc2  1250EDT \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du6i01gu5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
