\par\par \b \uc2  CORRECTED-Fed and BOJ alone on dlr/yen  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 -traders. \b0\par\par\uc2 358 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juni 1998\par 15:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  In London story headlined "Fed and BOJ alone on dlr/yen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 -traders" please read in first and second paragraphs that the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was selling not buying. \par \par \uc2  A corrected repetition follows. \par \par \uc2  LONDON, June 17 (Reuters) - The U.S. Federal Reserve and the Bank of Japan  stood alone in selling (corrects) dollars for yen on Wednesday, traders said. \par \par \uc2  They said there was no evidence that central banks from other countries had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  alongside the Fed to sell (corrects) dollars for yen at 139.10-15 and again with the Bank of Japan at 138.60 yen. \par \par \uc2  "There is absolutely no evidence that any other bank has been in the yen apart from the Fed," said one \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  salesman at a major European bank. \par \par \uc2  U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin confirmed the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in cooperation with Japanese authorities and said the U.S. was prepared to continue to cooperate in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  comes one day before a meeting between U.S. Deputy Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers and New York Federal Reserve President William McDonough with Bank of Japan and the Japanese government. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers in Europe said they saw no signs of any other banks involved in the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid a raft of "no comment" responses from central banks around the world. \par \par \uc2  "We think if this was concerted, the central banks would be making a lot more out of it, not just a bunch of 'no comments'," said one French trader. \par \par \uc2  In Frankfurt, traders said they saw no sign of the German \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Bundesbank itself declined to comment. \par \par \uc2  "We don't comment on such issues, we have nothing to say," a Bundesbank spokesman said in response to a Reuters enquiry. \par \par \uc2  The central banks of Germany, England, France, Italy, Sweden, and \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to comment on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while the central banks of Switzerland, Denmark and The Netherlands all said they had not participated. \par \par \uc2  ((Paul Casciato, London newsroom +44 171 542 8968 fax +44 171 542 5293, uk.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 .news@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6h02qa8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
