\par\par \b \uc2  Bank of Canada buys Canada dlr at C$1.4740-traders. \b0\par\par\uc2 163 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juni 1998\par 17:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TORONTO, June 15 (Reuters) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Monday morning and bought Canadian dollars for U.S. dollars from C$1.4730 (US$0.6789) up to C$1.4740 (US$0.6784), traders said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's action followed the Canadian unit's continuing slide versus the U.S. dollar, which was surging against key \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , particularly against the yen. \par \par \uc2  "There have been some flows coming out of Europe to sell \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," one trader said. \par \par \uc2  And the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has helped slow down the U.S. dollar's one-way rise, he said. \par \par \uc2  "If it weren't there, the dollar/Canada would be a bit higher, probably at C$1.4760 or so," he said, adding that corporate buying of Canada would emerge at that level. \par \par \uc2  ((Reuters Toronto newsroom (416) 941-8107, toronto.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6f033z1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
