\par\par \b \uc2  Canada dlr hits new low against U.S. dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 333 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juni 1998\par 16:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TORONTO, June 15 (Reuters) - The Canadian dollar continued to weaken against the U.S. dollar on Monday morning, hitting another intraday weak point of C$1.4728 (US$0.6790), traders said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had set a new low of C$1.4715 (US$0.6796) about an hour earlier as the market tested the topside of the U.S. dollar in the absence of clear signs that \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the local dollar. \par \par \uc2  Traders said they expected the Canadian dollar to weaken further. \par \par \uc2  They reckoned the Bank of Canada would not raise its key lending rate to boost the local dollar by attracting investors through higher returns on Canadian assets. \par \par \uc2  "The market consensus seems to be that they (the Bank of Canada) won't do anything any time soon," said Reid Farrill, executive director, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at CIBC Wood Gundy Securities. \par \par \uc2  Canada's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last raised its bank rate by 50 basis points to 5.0 percent on January 30 after the local dollar had plunged on speculative selling and spurred monetary conditions considered too loose. \par \par \uc2  By the bank's measure, a weaker Canadian dollar means more stimulus in the domestic economy as it lowers export prices. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the Canadian unit firmed against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in cross trading, rising to 99.24 yen from 98.35 yen late on Friday here. \par \par \uc2  The yen has been hit by the growing concern over the stagnant Japanese economy and Asia's economic problems. \par \par \uc2  Against the German mark, the Canadian dollar shed earlier gains and was quoted around 1.2308 marks, down from 1.2311 marks in late North American trade on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar continued to surge versus the yen and mark on the back of a safe-haven flight of capital to U.S. markets from Asia and part of Europe. \par \par \uc2  ((Reuters Toronto newsroom (416) 941-8100, toronto.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6f033do\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
