\par\par \b \uc2  Canada dollar opens weaker in range trade. \b0\par\par\uc2 628 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juni 1998\par 14:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  FORECAST RANGE   1.4660/1.4730     ASIAN CLOSE    1.4686 \par \par \uc2  US$ SUPPORT 1.4640 RESISTANCE 1.4750 HIGH 1.4703 LOW 1.4674 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par CANADA OPEN 1.4699 HIGH 1.4700\tab EUROPE OPEN    1.4684\par PREV CLOSE  1.4665 LOW  1.4689\tab HIGH 1.4698 LOW 1.4662\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -----------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par MONDAY, JUNE 15\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TREND: NEUTRAL ACTIVITY: MODERATE\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Canada dollar opened weaker at C$1.4699 (US$0.6803), trading\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in a tight range and retaining bearish tone from overseas.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * USD continued to rise above 146 yen on Asian economic concerns and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par above 1.81 marks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TORONTO, June 15 (Reuters) - The Canadian dollar opened weaker at C$1.4699 (US$0.6803), retaining the weakness from overseas.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Later the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hit a new low against the U.S. dollar around C$1.4715 (US$0.6796) in nervous trading.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par This follows the U.S. dollar's continuous gain against major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , particularly the slumping Japanese yen, as concern over Asia's economic problems fuelled safe-haven capital shifts to U.S. dollar assets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In cross trading, however, the Canadian unit rose to 1.2332 marks from 1.2311 marks at the previous close here, and to 99.34 yen from 98.35 yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par There was no indication of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  this morning, traders said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The previous low of C$1.4711 (US$0.6798) was set on Thursday, June 11.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The U.S. dollar continued to surge against the yen, touching an eight-year high of 146.55 yen overnight as jitters over Japan's economic health and Asian market declines grew.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    "I think the (\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central) bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  seems unconcerned at the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par moment," said one trader. "The trend is still for a weaker\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (Canadian) \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , so I don't think there's any reason to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stop levels. The market is going to trade carefully around a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par potential for the Bank of Canada to come in."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    The market is expected to buy U.S. dollars on any dips, the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trader said. "Nobody really wants to get caught too short," he\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The latest data confirmed that Japan was deep in recession.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Its gross domestic product contracted at an annual rate of 5.3\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent in the first quarter after a revised annualized drop of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1.5 percent in the previous quarter.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Canada remained under pressure from soft commodities\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par prices, which have also hit the Australian and New Zealand\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollars. Canada's Asian exposure is more limited, but it is\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par vulnerable to volatility in such \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  because of a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par perception it shares a similar dependency on commodities.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Australian dollar was quoted around US$0.5864, down\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from US$0.5885 in late Friday trade here, and the New Zealand\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar around US$0.4949, down from US$0.5003.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Key economic indicators for next week:\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Tuesday, June 16\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    U.S. May consumer price index (CPI) forecast +0.2 percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par after +0.2 percent in April, and the core rate (ex-food and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par energy) +0.2 percent after +0.3 percent in April.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     U.S. May industrial output forecast at +0.4 percent after\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par +0.1 percent in April.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Canada's April Manufacturing shipments forecast +0.8\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent after +0.9 percent in March.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Thursday, June 18\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Canada's April merchandise trade surplus forecast C$1.69\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par billion, up from C$1.56 billion in March\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Friday, June 19\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Canada's May CPI forecast +0.7 percent in all items year on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par year after +0.8 percent in April, and +1.2 percent in core\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (ex-food and energy) after +1.2 percent in April.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (Masaru Sato, Reuters Toronto newsroom (416) 941-8107,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par toronto.newsroom@reuters.com))\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6f02t3g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgo