\par\par \b \uc2  Canada dollar weaker, hits new low by midday. \b0\par\par\uc2 852 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juni 1998\par 18:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  FORECAST RANGE   1.4660/1.4750     ASIAN CLOSE    1.4686 \par \par \uc2  US$ SUPPORT 1.4640 RESISTANCE 1.4800 HIGH 1.4703 LOW 1.4674 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par CANADA OPEN 1.4699 HIGH 1.4740\tab EUROPE OPEN    1.4684\par PREV CLOSE  1.4665 LOW  1.4689\tab HIGH 1.4698 LOW 1.4662\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -----------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par MONDAY, JUNE 15\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TREND: BEARISH ACTIVITY: ACTIVE\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par *The Canadian dollar continued to weaken, quoted at C$1.4737 (US$0.6786) at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par midday. *It hit another intra-day low of around C$1.4740 (US$0.6784) in morning\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trade, and the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to buy CAD at levels C$1.4730,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par C$1.4735 and C$1.4740. *USD stayed above 146 yen and 1.81, attracting\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par safe-haven buying.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TORONTO, June 15 (Reuters) - The Canadian dollar continued to weaken on Monday, quoted at C$1.4699 (US$0.6803) at midday, after hitting a new intra-day low around C$1.4740 (US$0.6784).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A wave of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to buy Canadian dollars for U.S. dollars at five-point intervals from C$1.4730 (US$0.6789) up to C$1.4740 (US$0.6784) helped slow the Canadian dollar's slide.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par One trader estimated the size of each shot by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at US$40-US$50 million, a level that is not out of the ordinary for such \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The overall outlook for the Canadian unit remained bleak as concern over Asia's economic problems continued to spur safe-haven capital flows into U.S. dollar assets and soft commodities prices overhung Canada.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Until you start to see it (the U.S. dollar) come off below C$1.4700 (US$0.6803) to figure, I think people with long U.S. dollar (positions) will keep them," the trader said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The battered Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , however, firmed against the Japanese yen in cross trading, rising to 99.42 yen from 98.35 yen late on Friday here.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The yen has been hit by the growing concern over the stagnant Japanese economy and Asia's financial problems.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Against the German mark, the Canadian dollar shed earlier gains and was quoted around 1.2303 marks, down from 1.2311 marks in late North American trade on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    "There have been some flows coming out of Europe to sell \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," the trader\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     And the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has helped slow down the U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  dollar's one-way rise, he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "If it weren't there, the dollar/Canada would be a bit higher, probably at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par C$1.4760 (US$0.6775) or so," he said, adding that corporate buying of Canada\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par would emerge at that level.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Traders expect the Bank of Canada to hold off from raising its key lending\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rate to boost the local dollar by attracting investors through higher returns\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on Canadian assets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "The market consensus seems to be that they (the Bank of Canada) won't do\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par anything any time soon," said Reid Farrill, executive director, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign\par \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 \par exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at CIBC Wood Gundy Securities.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Canada's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last raised its bank rate by 50 basis points to 5.0\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent on January 30 after the local dollar had plunged on speculative selling\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and spurred monetary conditions considered too loose.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By the bank's measure, a weaker Canadian dollar means more stimulus in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par domestic economy as it lowers export prices.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The latest data confirmed Japan was deep in recession. Its gross domestic\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par product contracted at an annual rate of 5.3 percent in the first quarter after\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a revised annualized drop of 1.5 percent in the previous quarter.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Canada remained under pressure from soft commodities prices, which have\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par also hit the Australian and New Zealand dollars. Canada's Asian exposure is\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par more limited, but it is vulnerable to volatility in such \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  because of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a perception it shares a similar dependency on commodities.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Australian dollar was quoted around US$0.5882, little changed from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par US$0.5885 in late Friday trade here, and the New Zealand dollar around\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par US$0.4970, down from US$0.5003.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Key economic indicators for the week:\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Tuesday, June 16\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    U.S. May consumer price index (CPI) forecast +0.2 percent after +0.2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent in April, and the core rate (ex-food and energy) +0.2 percent after\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par +0.3 percent in April.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     U.S. May industrial output forecast at +0.4 percent after +0.1 percent in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par April.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Canada's April Manufacturing shipments forecast +0.8 percent after +0.9\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent in March.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Thursday, June 18\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Canada's April merchandise trade surplus forecast C$1.69 billion, up from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par C$1.56 billion in March\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Friday, June 19\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Canada's May CPI forecast +0.7 percent in all items year on year after +0.8\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent in April, and +1.2 percent in core (ex-food and energy) after +1.2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent in April.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     (Masaru Sato, Reuters Toronto newsroom (416) 941-8107,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par toronto.newsroom@reuters.com))\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6f02sbf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
