\par\par \b \uc2  Canada dollar opens a bit firmer in quiet trade. \b0\par\par\uc2 590 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 1998\par 15:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  FORECAST RANGE   1.4610/1.4670     ASIAN CLOSE    1.4651 \par \par \uc2  US$ SUPPORT 1.4550 RESISTANCE 1.4700 HIGH 1.4669 LOW 1.4643 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par CANADA OPEN 1.4643 HIGH 1.4646\tab EUROPE OPEN    1.4640\par PREV CLOSE  1.4658 LOW  1.4638\tab HIGH 1.4655 LOW 1.4640\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -----------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par THURSDAY, JUNE 11\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TREND: NEUTRAL ACTIVITY: MODERATE\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par *Canadian dollar opened a bit firmer at C$1.4643 (US$0.6829)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in quiet trade. *No strong interest seen in testing CAD record\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par intra-day low vs USD of 1.4686 (US$0.6809) set Jan 29. *USD\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par firm vs mark and yen. *Japan stocks, bonds, yen all tumbled in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tokyo overnight.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TORONTO, June 11 (Reuters) - The Canadian dollar opened a bit firmer at C$1.4643 (US$0.6829) on Thursday in quiet trade after Wednesday's selling subsided.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  remains vulnerable to any erratic moves in sister \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of commodities export-oriented economies, such as Australia and New Zealand.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The flight-to-quality capital flows from Asia into the United States benefit Canada's long-term bonds, but not the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "We're going to drift off again, but I don't think today is for a new high or anything," said one trade. "We are going to watch Aussie and Kiwi. As long as they are stable, I think Canada will maintain some kind of stability as well."\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market on Wednesday to buy Canadian dollars from C$1.4655 (US$0.6824) to C$1.4675 (US$0.6814), preventing a further decline.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Canadian dollar hit a record intra-day low versus the U.S. dollar of C$1.4686 (US$0.6809) on January 29 this year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bank of Canada Senior Deputy Governor Bernard Bonin speaks to the Canadian Association of Financial Planners in Quebec City today, starting at 1300 EDT/1700 GMT. He's expected to discuss the bank's latest economic outlook in its semi-annual monetary policy report published in May.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In cross trading, the Canadian dollar continued to rise to 1.2297 marks from 1.2244 marks at the previous close here, and to 96.69 yen from 96.46 yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The U.S. dollar was firmer against the mark and yen in North American trade. Concern over Asia is helping buying of U.S. dollars. The Japanese market saw a triple decline in stocks, bonds and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  overnight.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    The Australian and New Zealand dollars were steady after a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rebound on Wednesday. The Aussie, after hitting 12-year lows\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par this week, was quoted around US$0.5905 in North American trade.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  The kiwi was quoted around US$0.5010 after hitting a near\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 12-year trough of US$0.4918 on Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     U.S. data this morning showed the economy was showing a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par steady rate of growth.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     U.S. May retail sales rose 0.9 percent after a revised\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0.7-percent increase in April. Ex-auto sales rose 0.4 percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par after rising 0.5 percent in April.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Economists on average had forecast a 0.7-percent rise in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par May after a preliminary 0.5-percent rise in April.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     For inflation outlook, the U.S. producer price index for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par May will be released on Friday. Economists on average expect\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par both the overall and core PPI to rise 0.1 percent after a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0.2-percent rise in April.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     (Masaru Sato, Reuters Toronto newsroom (416) 941-8107,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par toronto.newsroom@reuters.com))\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6b036so\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
