\par\par \b \uc2  Canada dollar ends weak after hitting intraday low. \b0\par\par\uc2 814 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 1998\par 22:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  FORECAST RANGE   1.4610/1.4670     ASIAN CLOSE    1.4651 \par \par \uc2  US$ SUPPORT 1.4550 RESISTANCE 1.4700 HIGH 1.4669 LOW 1.4643 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par CANADA OPEN 1.4643 HIGH 1.4711\tab EUROPE OPEN    1.4640\par PREV CLOSE  1.4658 LOW  1.4638\tab HIGH 1.4655 LOW 1.4640\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -----------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par THURSDAY, JUNE 11\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TREND: WEAKER ACTIVITY: ACTIVE\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par *Canadian dollar was weaker around C$1.4690 (US$0.6807), but\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par recovered from a record intra-day low vs USD of C$1.4711\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (US$0.6798). *USD surged vs major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as market took\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. Treasury Sec Rubin's comments as an indication that G7\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par will take no joint action to stem yen's slide. *Rubin told\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Senate banking committee that while weak yen is global concern,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par remedy lies in hands of Japanese policymakers. *Rubin later\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  not off table, U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would come\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par at appropriate timing. *Japan said overnight G7 coordination on\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  still intact. *Bank of Canada Senior Deputy Governor\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bonin's comment that Canada's recent monetary conditions\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par appropriate for coming months triggered mild CAD selling.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TORONTO, June 11 (Reuters) - The Canadian dollar ended weaker at C$1.4694 (US$0.6805) on Thursday, after hitting a new low in the absence of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Not only the Canadian but also the Japanese and German \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  all slumped as the U.S. dollar powered ahead on the back of safe-haven capital flows from Asia into the United States.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Canadian dollar hit a record intra-day low of C$1.4711 (US$0.6798) against the the U.S. dollar in afternoon trade, slipping below the previous all-time low of C$1.4686 (US$0.6809) on January 29.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In cross trading, however, the Canadian unit continued to rise to 1.2304 marks from 1.2244 marks at the previous close here, and jumped to 98.01 yen from 96.46 yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The U.S. dollar also surged on comments by U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin, which were taken as indications that Group of Seven (G7) major industrialised nations have no plans for joint action to help stem yen's slide.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Rubin told the Senate banking committee that while the weak yen is a global concern, the remedy for it is in the hands of Japanese policymakers.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par By contrast, Japan said overnight that G7 coordination on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  issue is still intact.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Rubin later told the committee that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is not off the table and that U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would come when the time is appropriate.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par At one point, comments by a Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  official triggered mild selling of the Canadian dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bank of Canada Senior Deputy Governor Bernard Bonin on Thursday said Canada's monetary policy should remain on hold for the next five months, barring any blows to the economy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The market took this to mean that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would not raise rates to help the falling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  through higher returns on investment in Canadian assets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "People got nervous on it and the dollar moved about 15 points," one trader said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He expects the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to smooth the market around C$1.4725/30 (US$0.6791/0.6789).\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market on Wednesday to buy Canadian dollars from C$1.4655 (US$0.6824) to C$1.4675 (US$0.6814), which helped slow the slide.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par There was no indication that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  today.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    The Canadian dollar is under additional pressure from soft\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par commodities prices, which have also hit the Australian and New\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Zealand dollars.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Canada's Asian exposure is more limited, but it is\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par vulnerable to volatility in such \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  because of a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par perception that it shares a similar dependency on commodities.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Australian and New Zealand dollars were steady after a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rebound on Wednesday. The Aussie, after hitting 12-year lows\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par this week, was quoted around US$0.5847 in North American trade.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The kiwi was quoted around US$0.4947 after hitting a near\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 12-year trough of US$0.4918 on Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     U.S. data this morning showed the economy was showing a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par steady rate of growth.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The U.S. May retail sales rose 0.9 percent after a revised\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0.7-percent increase in April. Ex-auto sales rose 0.4 percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par after rising 0.5 percent in April.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Economists on average had forecast a 0.7-percent rise in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par May after a preliminary 0.5-percent rise in April.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     On the inflation outlook, the U.S. producer price index for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par May will be released on Friday. Economists on average expect\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par both the overall and core PPI to rise 0.1 percent after a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0.2-percent rise in April.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     (Masaru Sato, Reuters Toronto newsroom (416) 941-8107,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par toronto.newsroom@reuters.com))\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6b035si\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
