\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada Intervenes \highlight\uc2  -2: Cdn Dlr Near All-time Low \b0\par\par\uc2 297 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juni 1998\par 16:38\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Wednesday to sell U.S. dollars at\par C$1.4655 at around 10:20 a.m. EST (1420 GMT) in an effort to\par smooth out trading action, said a trader in Toronto.\par    The U.S. dollar's upward climb stalled after the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and was at C$1.4654 at 10:34 a.m. EDT (1434\par GMT).\par    The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's unofficial policy is to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets after intraday moves in either direction of\par about 70 ticks or more. The U.S. dollar closed at C$1.4586\par Wednesday.\par    The Canadian dollar has been under sustained negative\par pressure in recent weeks from a variety of factors, including\par commodity prices pushed lower by the continued economic and\par financial tumult in Asia and sustained negative yield spreads\par with the U.S.\par    The U.S. dollar climbed persistently higher on Wednesday\par morning, approaching its all-time high against the\par Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of C$1.4684.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Some analysts contend it is essential for the Bank of\par Canada to raise rates to bring an end to the persistent\par weakness in the Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    While the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  signalled in its semi-annual\par monetary policy report in May that current monetary\par conditions will likely be appropriate for the next six\par months, Governor Gordon Thiessen has also said the bank would\par defend the Canadian dollar in the event of a "crisis in\par confidence" in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    The day after the U.S. dollar hit its historic high of\par C$1.4684 on Jan. 29, the Bank of Canada raised its\par trendsetting bank rate 50 basis points to 5.00%.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires  06-10-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1038EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  4346 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du6a01glj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
