\par\par \b \uc2  Bank of Canada buys Canadian dlrs, traders say. \b0\par\par\uc2 129 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juni 1998\par 16:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TORONTO, June 10 (Reuters) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and bought Canadian dollars for U.S. dollars at C$1.4655 (US$0.6824) to defend the weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  move was widely anticipated as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to weaken after opening at C$1.4624 (US$0.6838), down from Tuesday's close of C$1.4588 (US$0.6855). \par \par \uc2  The Canadian dollar hit a record low against the U.S. dollar of C$1.4686 (US$0.6809) on January 29 this year, when it came under speculative selling pressure. \par \par \uc2  ((Reuters Toronto Newsroom, 416 941-8100, Fax 416 869-3436, toronto.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6a03cih\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
