\par\par \b \uc2  Canada dollar weaker at midday despite BOC buying. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,099 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juni 1998\par 18:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  FORECAST RANGE   1.4600/1.4660     ASIAN CLOSE    1.4625 \par \par \uc2  US$ SUPPORT 1.4500 RESISTANCE 1.4680 HIGH 1.4633 LOW 1.4579 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par CANADA OPEN 1.4624 HIGH 1.4666\tab EUROPE OPEN    1.4626\par PREV CLOSE  1.4588 LOW  1.4620\tab HIGH 1.4633 LOW 1.4583\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -----------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par WEDNESDAY, JUNE 10\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TREND: WEAKER ACTIVITY: ACTIVE\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par *The Canadian dollar continued to weaken, quoted at C$1.4666 (US$0.6818) at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par midday and creeping down to record low vs USD of 1.4686 (US$0.6809) marked in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par January. *The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to sell USD C$1.4655 (US$0.6824),\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trying to prevent CAD from falling further. *U.S. and Canada long bonds surge\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on Greenspan comments that Fed needs no credit tightening yet. *USD powering\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ahead towards 142 yen and 1.80 marks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TORONTO, June 10 (Reuters) - The Canadian dollar continued to weaken at midday on Wednesday despite rounds of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  aimed at preventing a further fall in the depressed \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was buying Canadian dollars at every five-point interval from C$1.4655 (US$0.6824) to C$1.4675 (US$0.6814), one trader said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Some selling of Canadian dollars by U.S. accounts was noted at midday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par As the U.S. dollar surged against major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the wake of safe-haven buying, the Canadian unit continued to slip after opening at C$1.4624 (US$0.6838), down from Tuesday's close at C$1.4588 (US$0.6855).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In cross trading, however, the Canadian dollar was rising to 1.2249 marks from 1.2201 marks at the previous close here, and to 96.42 yen from 96.12 yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The U.S. dollar was marching towards 142 yen and 1.80 marks against the backdrop of safe-haven capital flows into the United States from Asia's troubled economies and markets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Canadian dollar hit a record low versus the U.S. dollar at C$1.4686 (US$0.6809) on January 29 this year, when it came under speculative selling.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In a prepared speech, U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan said the Fed has not yet seen a need to tighten monetary policy, but that it is watching inflation closely.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par This propelled North American long bond buying.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  benefited from the Greenspan testimony as dealers thought he was suggesting a rate increase, which would attract investors with higher yields.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Greenspan also said the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might need to raise interest rates unless U.S. demand abates "noticeably."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Fed chief said the U.S. economy is expanding strongly despite a strong drag on trade.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He was testifying on monetary policy and the outlook for the U.S. economy before the joint economic committee of Congress. His testimony started around 1100 EDT/1500 GMT today.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    With the Australian dollar and the Japanese yen sinking to recent lows,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par speculator focus may be shifting to the Canadian dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The market has ignored Canada's fairly good economic fundamentals, steady\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par growth with low inflation, and has instead followed the flow of buying U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  dollars\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Strong U.S. jobs data and relatively weak Canadian employment numbers\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par released last Friday triggered selling of the Canadian dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "We are better than Australia, but that's no comfort to Canadians," said a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bank of Canada source. "I do feel that the (Canadian) dollar should be worth a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par little bit more."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Before taking policy action, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is watching if speculative\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par forces in the market are taking the Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  drastically down and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par whether the market is losing confidence in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Australian dollar was falling towards US$0.58 to the U.S. dollar, but\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rebounded to trade around US$0.5865.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Market players expect the bank to raise interest rates to attract investors\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with higher yields if the Canadian unit continues to drop sharply.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Bank policymakers have pointed out that they are not reacting to daily\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par movements and are looking at the overall monetary conditions. A weaker Canadian\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar contributes to looser monetary conditions in Canada.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Economic fundamentals have a tough time in the face of safe-haven capital\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par flows into U.S. dollar-denominated assets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Asian sharemarkets tumbled overnight on the growing fear of a falling yen\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and its impact on the Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The market tends to link the image of an Aussie dollar sell-off to Canada\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par selling, although Australian exports are much more exposed to the economic\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par slump in Asia than Canada's exports to the region, which represent less than 10\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent of the nation's total.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Obviously there's stops (stop-loss orders) at C$1.4610 (US$0.6845) taken\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par out overnight," said one trader. "There's broad-based (U.S.) dollar buying from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Far Eastern accounts and European accounts."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "There may be some stories going around that spec guys might have a look at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Canada and now trying to have a go at it and sell Canada," he said. "There's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par one or two U.S. investment types looking to sell U.S., so it's a little bit of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par two-way business going on at these levels here."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    The market is also looking for comments on exchange rates from the deputies\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to finance ministers from the Group of Seven major nations meeting in Paris.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     They are in Paris for the June 9-10 meeting of the Working Party III of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Organisation for Economic Cooperation and Development.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     A weak yen might be of help for Japan's stagnant economy as it makes\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Japanese exports cheaper, but that is a threat to exporters from other Asian\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par countries. Meanwhile, the strong U.S. dollar cuts import bills and helps curb\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. inflation.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On the strength of the U.S. economy, the market expects slightly stronger\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par retail sales on Thursday. Economists on average forecast a 0.7-percent rise in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par May after a 0.5-percent rise in April.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par For inflation outlook, the U.S. producer price index for May will be\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par released on Friday. Economists on average expect both the overall and core PPI\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to rise 0.1 percent after a 0.2-percent rise in April.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The policy-setting U.S. Federal Open Market Committee will meet on June 30\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and July 1. For the rest of the year, the FOMC is scheduled to meet on August\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 18, September 29, November 17, and December 22.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     (Masaru Sato, Reuters Toronto newsroom (416) 941-8107,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par toronto.newsroom@reuters.com))\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6a03be0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
