\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Canada \highlight\uc2  dollar weakens,  \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 1,074 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juni 1998\par 16:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  FORECAST RANGE   1.4600/1.4660     ASIAN CLOSE    1.4625 \par \par \uc2  US$ SUPPORT 1.4500 RESISTANCE 1.4680 HIGH 1.4633 LOW 1.4579 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par CANADA OPEN 1.4624 HIGH 1.4651\tab EUROPE OPEN    1.4626\par PREV CLOSE  1.4588 LOW  1.4620\tab HIGH 1.4633 LOW 1.4583\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -----------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par WEDNESDAY, JUNE 10\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TREND: WEAKER ACTIVITY: ACTIVE\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par *The Canadian dollar continued to weaken towards C$1.4655 (US$0.6824), where\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to sell USD, trying to defend CAD. *CAD's record\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par low vs the USD at 1.4686 (US$0.6809) is still ahead, and the market wants to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par see how determined the BOC is in defending CAD. *Market awaiting any \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par comments from G7 deputies meeting in Paris this week, and any hints for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par monetary policy direction from U.S. Fed Chairman Greenspan's testimony today at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par around 1100 EDT/1500 GMT. *USD was bid up to 141 yen and 1.7965 marks in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par morning trade.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TORONTO, June 10 (Reuters) - The Canadian dollar continued to weaken on Wednesday, and the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to defend the depressed \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by selling U.S. dollars at C$1.4655 (US$0.6824).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's move was widely anticipated as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  continued to weaken after opening at C$1.4624 (US$0.6838) this morning, down from Tuesday's close at C$1.4588 (US$0.6855).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Canadian dollar hit a record low versus the U.S. dollar at C$1.4686 (US$0.6809) on January 29 this year, when it came under speculative selling.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In a prepared speech, U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan said the Fed has not yet seen the need to tighten its monetary policy, but that it is watching inflation closely.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He said the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might need to raise interest rates unless U.S. demand abates "noticeably."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Greenspan also said the U.S. economy is expanding strongly despite a strong drag on trade.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He was testifying on monetary policy and the outlook for the U.S. economy before the joint economic committee of Congress started around 1100 EDT/1500 GMT today.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In cross trading, the Canadian dollar was afloat at 1.2235 marks, up from 1.2201 marks at the previous close here, and was at 96.32 yen, up from 96.12 yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The U.S. dollar continued to firm to around 141.25 yen and 1.7952 marks in morning trade.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Australian dollar was falling towards 0.58 to the U.S. dollar, but rebounded to trade around 0.5865 this morning.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Now that the Australian dollar and the Japanese yen have been sinking to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par new lows, an attack on the Canadian unit by speculators is feared.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The market has ignored Canada's fairly good economic fundamentals, steady\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par growth with low inflation, and instead followed the flow of buying the U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  dollar, which has been also firming against the yen and the mark.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "We are better than Australia, but that's no comfort to Canadians," said a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bank of Canada source. "I do feel that the (Canadian) dollar should be worth a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par little bit more."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Before taking policy action, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is watching if speculative\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par forces in the market are taking the Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  drastically down and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par whether the market is losing confidence in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Market players expect the bank to raise interest rates to attract investors\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with higher yields if the Canadian unit continues to drop sharply.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Bank policymakers have pointed out they are not reacting to daily movements\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and are looking at the overall monetary conditions. A weaker Canadian dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par contributes to looser monetary conditions in Canada.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Economic fundamentals have a tough time competing against safe-haven\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par capital flows into U.S. dollar-denominated assets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Asian sharemarkets tumbled overnight on the growing fear of a falling yen\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and its impact on the Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The market tends to link the image of an Aussie dollar sell-off to Canada\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par selling, although Australian exports are much more exposed to the economic\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par slump in Asia than Canada's exports to the region, which are less than 10\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent of the nation's total.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Obviously there's stops (stop-loss orders) at C$1.4610 (US$0.6845) taken\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par out overnight," said one trader. "There's broad-based (U.S.) dollar buying from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Far Eastern accounts and European accounts."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "There may be some stories going around that spec guys might have a look at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Canada and now trying to have a go at it and sell Canada," he said. "There's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par one or two U.S. investment types looking to sell U.S., so it's a little bit of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par two-way business going on at these levels here."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    The market wants to see the resolve of the Bank of Canada to defend the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par depressed \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "The market looks to the C$1.4605 (US$0.6847) level to buy some U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  dollars, and they will probably expect at some point to test the bank at the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par C$1.4660 (US$0.68121) level today," the trader said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The market is also looking for comments on exchange rates from deputy\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par finance ministers from the Group of Seven nations meeting in Paris.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     They are in Paris for the June 9-10 meeting of the Working Party III of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Organisation for Economic Cooperation and Development.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     A weak yen might help Japan's stagnant economy as it makes Japanese\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par exporters cheaper, but that is a threat to other exporting Asian countries.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Meanwhile, the strong U.S. dollar cuts import bills and helps curb U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par inflation.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On the strength of the U.S. economy, the market expects slightly stronger\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par retail sales on Thursday. Economists on average forecast a 0.7-percent rise in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par May after a 0.5-percent rise in April.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par For inflation outlook, the U.S. producer price index for May will be\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par released on Friday. Economists on average expect both the overall and core PPI\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to rise 0.1 percent after a 0.2-percent rise in April.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The policy-setting U.S. Federal Open Market Committee will meet on June 30\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and July 1. For the rest of the year, the FOMC is scheduled to meet on August\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 18, September 29, November 17, and December 22.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     (Masaru Sato, Reuters Toronto newsroom (416) 941-8107,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par toronto.newsroom@reuters.com))\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6a034qn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
