\par\par \b \uc2  Canada dollar opens a bit firmer. \b0\par\par\uc2 449 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Mai 1998\par 15:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par FORECAST RANGE   1.4510/1.4550\tab    ASIAN CLOSE   1.4544\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par RESISTANCE   1.4450 SUPPORT 1.4590     HI 1.4558  LO 1.4525\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par CANADA OPEN  1.4533   HI 1.4534\tab   EUROPE OPEN   1.4528\par PREV CLOSE   1.4539   LO 1.4525\tab   HI 1.4549  LO 1.4525\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -----------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par FRIDAY, MAY 29\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TREND: NEUTRAL. ACTIVITY: MODERATE *Canada dollar opened a bit\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par firmer at C$1.4533 ($0.6881), gaining on crosses overnight,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par particularly vs mark. *Germany's proximity to Russia's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par financial turmoil caused mark selling vs CAD and USD. *Before\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par profit-taking emerged this morning, USD rose vs yen overnight\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par as worries over Japan's economy deepened with its jobless rate\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rising to recent record of 4.1 percent in April.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TORONTO, May 29 (Reuters) - The Canadian dollar opened slightly firmer at C$1.4533 ($0.6881), gaining on the crosses overnight, particularly against the mark.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Germany's proximity to Russia's financial turmoil prompted mark selling against the U.S. and Canadian dollars.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Before profit-taking emerged this morning, the U.S. rose to touch 139 yen as worries over Japan's economy deepened.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Japan's jobless rate hit a record high of 4.1 percent in April, creeping up to the unemployment rate in the United States, which has fallen to 4.3 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On the crosses, the Canadian dollar rose to 1.2300 marks from 1.2234 marks at the previous close here, and to 95.45 yen from 95.38 yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The market lacked clear direction.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "For the last day and a half, the slide (in the Canadian\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar) has abated, but we're basically sitting here around\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par C$1.4540 (US$0.6878) area, waiting to see what's next," said\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Reid Farrill, executive director, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at CIBC Wood\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Gundy Securities. "It's hard to say what's really going to be\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the next factor to move the market."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Canada's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is warning the market there's no\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par absolute level for the monetary conditions index (MCI), which\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the market was watching for signs of bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  or\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par tightening aimed at defending its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Governor Gordon Thiessen has repeatedly said\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par there's no target zone for the Canadian dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Canadian dollar has not recovered from selling that was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sparked by the market perception that the the bank would leave\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par its accommodative monetary policy unchanged for the next six\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par months.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers were disappointed by the May 13 release of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bank's semi-annual policy report, which did not contain a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par much-sought-after bias towards credit tightening.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     (Masaru Sato, Reuters Toronto newsroom (416) 941-8107,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par toronto.newsroom@reuters.com))\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du5t0488f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
