\par\par \b \uc2  World  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  -2: Russia  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervenes \highlight\uc2  For Ruble \b0\par\par\uc2 337 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Mai 1998\par 23:19\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  In Russia, the ruble tumbled Tuesday, forcing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again in defense of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Investors bailed out of bonds and stocks on concerns that the government has no emergency plan to prop up its collapsing financial markets, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Russian Treasury bond (GKO) prices plummeted, sending the yield on GKOs as high as 57.0% from 50.0% a day ago and fueling speculation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will raise interest rates for the third time in less than a month. Last week, Russia raised its key interest rates to 50% to shore up the ruble against a massive exodus of foreign capital. \par \par \uc2  Late in Moscow, the dollar for next-day delivery was at 6.184 rubles, up from RUR6.174 Monday. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Mikhail Zadornov said Tuesday that despite the erosion of Russia's financial markets over the past week, the government isn't seeking additional international aid to stabilize the markets. He also said, "there will be no devaluation." \par \par \uc2  "But the German \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  wasn't the sole victim of Russia's troubles. In fact, fears of a ruble devaluation fueled a nervous selloff in emerging markets, with the Polish zloty and Czech koruna sustaining big losses. After a sharp decline Monday, the South African rand recovered against the dollar Tuesday." \par \par \uc2  The Canadian dollar also tumbled, prodding the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in an effort to arrest its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fall. Traders attributed the drop in part to soft global commodity prices and delayed pressure from the Bank of Canada's semi-annual monetary report, released weeks ago, in which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said monetary conditions will likely remain steady for the next six months. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also changing hands at C$1.4548, up from C$1.4492. \par \par \uc2  (For a fuller account of the day's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  activity, please turn to Dow Jones page 1033) \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 26-05-98 \par \par \uc2  2119GMT \par \par \uc2  (corrected 5:53 edt) \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du5q04hvk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
