\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Canada \highlight\uc2  Afternoon: C$ Tumbles, Bank of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada Intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 308 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Mai 1998\par 21:39\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Canadian dollar tumbled substantially lower Tuesday, prompting \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  in an effort to restrict market volatility. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar traded at C$1.4546 at 3:35 p.m. EDT (1935 GMT), from C$1.4517 at 8:00 a.m. EDT (1200 GMT), and from C$1.4490 late Monday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar jumped as high as C$1.4562 Tuesday afternoon, prompting the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in an effort to restrict market volatility. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold U.S. dollars at C$1.4560 at around 2 p.m. EDT (1800 GMT), after which the U.S. dollar levelled off and then subsided slightly. \par \par \uc2  Market sources cited a number of different factors behind the renewed downward pressure on the Canadian unit, which had been trading in a broad range between U.S. dollar levels of C$1.4400 and C$1.4500 in recent sessions. \par \par \uc2  Several sources cited selling pressures against a number of commodity-linked \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , such as the Australian and New Zealand dollars, and continuing negative yield spreads between Canada and the U.S. \par \par \uc2  The pressure stemming from the fact that Canadian yields remain lower than those in the U.S. has intensified in recent weeks after the Bank of Canada signalled in its semi-annual monetary policy report that monetary conditions in Canada will likely remain appropriate for the next six months, while fears of an impending interest rate increase from the U.S. Federal Reserve Board persist in some market circles. \par \par \uc2  One Toronto-based \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's downward spiral on Tuesday began with cross selling of the Canadian dollar against the Japanese yen in Europe. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 26-05-98 \par \par \uc2  1939GMT \par \par \uc2  1158 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du5q04ht2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
