\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada Intervenes \highlight\uc2  -2:  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Levels After Action \b0\par\par\uc2 236 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Mai 1998\par 20:32\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Tuesday afternoon to sell U.S. dollars at C$1.4560 in an effort to smooth out trading action, said a trader in Toronto. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar leveled off at around C$1.4554 after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  came after the Canadian dollar slid substantially Tuesday morning, with the U.S. dollar climbing to the C$1.4560 level by early afternoon from its Monday close of C$1.4492. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's unofficial policy is to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets after intraday moves in either direction of 70 ticks or more in order to contain volatility. \par \par \uc2  The Canadian dollar has been under pressure in recent weeks from a variety of factors, including weakness in commodity prices and sustained negative yield spreads between Canada and the U.S. \par \par \uc2  It lost significant ground earlier in May when the Bank of Canada released its semi-annual monetary policy report. The report indicated that current monetary conditions are "broadly appropriate" for the next six months in the absence of any unexpected economic shocks. \par \par \uc2  Many market participants interpreted the statement as implying that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not be raising interest rates in that period, resulting in additional pressure for the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires  05-26-98 \par \par \uc2  1432EDT \par \par \uc2  4346 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du5q01awd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
