\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada Intervenes \highlight\uc2  -2: BOC Report Pushes C$ Down \b0\par\par\uc2 272 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Mai 1998\par 16:34\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Wednesday to sell U.S. dollars at\par C$1.4410 shortly before 10:00 a.m. EDT (1400 GMT) in an effort\par to smooth out trading action, said a trader in Toronto.\par    The U.S. dollar surged immediately after the release of the\par Bank of Canada's semi-annual monetary policy report at 9:30\par a.m. EDT (1330 GMT), jumping from around C$1.4350 before the\par release to the C$1.4400 range shortly before 10:00 a.m. EDT.\par    Analysts said the crucial element in the report was a\par statement that the current level of monetary conditions will be\par appropriate for the next six months, given the prospect of\par slowing economic growth.\par    That statement was interpreted as suggesting that the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will not be increasing interest rates soon.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    "The one bit of news is the statement that the current\par level of monetary conditions is appropriate for the next six\par months, which I think will disappoint anyone holding the\par Canadian dollar waiting for a rate hike," said Avery Shenfeld,\par senior economist with CIBC Wood Gundy Inc.\par    Many analysts believe that the Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will stay\par weak as long as Canadian interest rates remain lower than those\par in the U.S.\par    The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's unofficial policy is to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets after intraday moves in either direction of 70\par ticks or more in order to contain volatility. The U.S. dollar\par closed at C$1.4340 Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires  05-13-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1034EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du5d018ym\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
