\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TORONTO, May 13 (Reuters) - The Canadian dollar slumped towards C$1.4430 (US$0.6930) after the Bank of Canada in its semi-annual report presented a view on growth and inflation that was taken as a neutral monetary policy stance.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stepped in and bought the Canadian unit for U.S. dollars at C$1.4410 (US$0.6940) in a bid to stem further falls, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The key phrase in the conclusion calls for neutral monetary conditions for the next six months," said Mark Chandler, senior economist at Goldman Sachs Canada. "Something certainly changed their view of the world, maybe through productivity increases.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The market had expected the bank to show a tighter money policy stance.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "In the near term, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is going to come under pressure, and we have to wait and see the Canada-U.S. spread," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par While the U.S. dollar is receiving underlying support from an widely expected Federal Reserve bias to credit tightening, the Canadian dollar lacks such support at the moment.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Expectations of higher interest rates usually support a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as capital tends to move to higher-yielding assets, and a lack of such expectations could hurt the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par It its semi-annual monetary policy report, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said recent monetary conditions in Canada would be "broadly appropriate" for the next six months.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also said Canadian economic growth in 1998 would not be as vigorous as thought before and that Canada's inflation should remain in the lower half of the target range of 1-3 percent for the next six months. He said the main downside risks for Canada are Asia's financial crisis and soft commodities prices.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  opened at C$1.4348 (US$0.6970) today, little changed from Tuesday's North American closing.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOC Governor Gordon Thiessen briefs on the report at 1100\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par EDT/1500 GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Key U.S. inflation data released today showed slightly\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par higher-than-expected\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rises, but U.S. inflation is still considered benign.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     U.S. April retail sales rose 0.5 percent (consensus forecast\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par +0.3 percent),\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ex-autos up 0.5 percent (+0.5 percent). The April producer price\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par index (PPI)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was up 0.2 percent (+0.1 percent) and the core rate was up 0.2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent (+0.2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Economists told Reuters Television it was hard to say\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par whether U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par inflation was on an upward trend just by looking at these\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par numbers, and thus the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was unlikely to raise rates at its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par policy-setting committee\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par meeting next Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Canada's March new motor vehicle sales rose 5.0 percent,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par compared with a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par consensus forecast of an increase of 6.5 percent. It was the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par second straight\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par gains after a decline in January.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On Thursday, Canada's April consumer price index (+1.0\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent y/y vs 0.9\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent in March) will be released at 0700 EDT/1100 GMT and the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. CPI (+0.2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent vs flat) at 0830 EDT/1230 GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On the crosses, the Canadian dollar shed earlier gains and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fell to 1.2314\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par marks from 1.2382 marks at the previous close here, and slipped\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to 92.90 yen\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from 93.31 yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The U.S. dollar eased versus the mark and yen. Earlier\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par renewed worries over\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Asia helped the safe-haven U.S. dollar trading higher. The clash\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par between\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Indonesian security forces and demonstrators resulted in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par deaths of six\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par students in Jakarta on Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     ((Masaru Sato, Reuters Toronto newsroom (416) 941-8107,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par toronto.newsroom@reuters.com))\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du5d05guo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
