\par expectations. *U.S. April retail sales +0.5 pct (fcast +0.3\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pct), ex-autos +0.5\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pct (+0.5 pct), April PPI +0.2 pct (+0.1 pct), core rate +0.2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pct (+0.2 pct).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TORONTO, May 13 (Reuters) - The Canadian dollar continued to slip to C$1.4444 (US$0.6923) by midday despite a wave of Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stem the fall.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Aggressive selling, triggered by the bank's published neutral monetary policy stance, has subsided after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had lost about one Canadian cent to the U.S. dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appeared to have stepped in at various levels at C$1.4410 (US$0.6940), C$1.4415 (US$0.6937), C$1.4425 (US$0.6932), C$1.4430 (US$0.6930), C$14440 (US$0.6925), and possibly C$1.4450 (US$0.6920), dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "If the market wants to take on speculative positions, it will put stops a little bit higher," said one dealer. "If we go above C$1.4455 (US$0.6918), I think they (the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) will come around C$1.4460/65 (US$0.6916/13) again. But right now it seems to be trading in a C$1.4430/50 (US$0.6930/20) range for the time being."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par It its semi-annual monetary policy report, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said recent monetary conditions in Canada would be "broadly appropriate" for the next six months.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The bank also said Canadian economic growth in 1998 would not be as vigorous as thought before, Canada's inflation should remain in the lower half of the target range of 1-3 percent for the next six months, and that main downside risks for Canada are Asia's financial crisis and soft commodities prices.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par While the U.S. dollar is receiving underlying support from an widely expected Federal Reserve credit tightening bias, the Canadian dollar lacks such support at the moment.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Expectations of higher interest rates usually support the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as capital tends to move to high-yielder assets, and a lack of such anticipation could hurt the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  opened at C$1.4348 (US$0.6970) today, little changed from Tuesday's North American closing.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     After this morning's sell-off, some see support for the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par battered Canadian\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par unit.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Susan Stearns, director, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at Bank of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Montreal in New York,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par told Reuters Television that she would go Canada long at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par C$1.4465 (US$0.6913)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par today.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Randall Powley, senior economist at Scotia Capital Markets,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should rebound and move in a range for the next two\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par months until\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par strong buying incentive emerges.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On how to read the report, Rob Palombi, senior fixed-income\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par analyst at MMS\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par International, warned that the Bank of Canada's neutral position\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par does not\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par necessarily mean it will not act before the next report is\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par published in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par November.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "If Asia doesn't weigh down the economy and the U.S. economy\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par doesn't slow\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par down, then there will be a reason for the bank to raise before\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the next\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par monetary policy report, he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will come under pressure in the near term, and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the market\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par should seek further direction from the spread between Canadian\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and U.S. yields,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said Mark Chandler, senior economist at Goldman Sachs Canada.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The key phrase in the conclusion calls for neutral monetary\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par conditions for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the next six months," he said. "Something certain changed their\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par view of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par world, maybe through productivity increases.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The market had expected the bank to show a tighter money\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par policy stance.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Key U.S. inflation-gauging data showed slightly\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par higher-than-expected rises,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par but the U.S. inflation is still considered benign.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     U.S. April retail sales rose 0.5 percent (consensus forecast\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par +0.3 percent),\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ex-autos up 0.5 percent (+0.5 percent). April producer price\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par index (PPI) was up\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0.2 percent (+0.1 percent), the core rate up 0.2 percent (+0.2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Economists told Reuters Television that it was hard to say\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par whether U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par inflation was on an upward trend just by looking at these\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par numbers, and thus the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was unlikely to raise rates at the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par policy-setting committee\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par meeting next Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Canada's March new motor vehicle sales rose 5.0 percent,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par compared with a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par consensus forecast of an increase of 6.5 percent. It was the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par second straight\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par gains after a decline in January.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On Thursday Canada's April consumer price index (+1.0\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent y/y vs 0.9\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent in March) will be released at 0700 EDT/1100 GMT and the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. CPI (+0.2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent vs flat) at 0830 EDT/1230 GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On the crosses, the Canadian dollar shed earlier gains and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fell to 1.2303\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par marks from 1.2382 marks at the previous close here, and slipped\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to 92.73 yen\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from 93.31 yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The U.S. dollar was buoyed by jitters over Asia. The clash\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par between\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Indonesian security forces and demonstrators resulted in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par deaths of six\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par students in Jakarta on Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     ((Masaru Sato, Reuters Toronto newsroom (416) 941-8107,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par toronto.newsroom@reuters.com))\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du5d05dc5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
