\par\par \b \uc2  Canada dollar ends little changed in range trade. \b0\par\par\uc2 601 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Mai 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par FORECAST RANGE   1.4360/1.4420\tab \tab ASIAN CLOSE   1.4397\par RESISTANCE   1.4270  SUPPORT 1.4450\tab  HI 1.4410  LO 1.4378\par CANADA OPEN  1.4383  HI 1.4410\tab \tab EUROPE OPEN   1.4388\par PREV CLOSE   1.4390  LO 1.4369\tab \tab HI 1.4408  LO 1.4373\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ---------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  WEDNESDAY, MAY 6 \par \par \uc2  TREND: NEUTRAL. ACTIVITY: MODERATE \par \par \uc2  *The Canadian dollar ended little changed around C$1.4386 \par \par \uc2  (US$0.6951) after \par \par \uc2  moving in tight band. *USD top-heavy at C$1.4410 (US$0.6940) for \par \par \uc2  now, while \par \par \uc2  it's testing topside above 133 yen. *In early trade, speculation \par \par \uc2  of a BOC rate \par \par \uc2  rise helped prop up CAD, but there was no sign of BOC stepping \par \par \uc2  in to stem CAD's \par \par \uc2  fall at this level. *Market is awaiting U.S. April jobs data \par \par \uc2  Friday for further \par \par \uc2  hint of U.S. inflation trends, thus Fed policy. *Looking ahead, \par \par \uc2  BOC issues its \par \par \uc2  semi-annual monetary policy report May 13. \par \par \uc2      TORONTO, May 6 (Reuters) - The Canadian dollar ended steady \par \par \uc2  at C$1.4391 (US$0.6949), staying in a tight band. \par \par \uc2      In early trade, speculation the Bank of Canada would raise a \par \par \uc2  key lending \par \par \uc2  rate to stem the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fall provided support, but there was \par \par \uc2  no sign of the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepping in either through raising rates or selling \par \par \uc2  U.S. \par \par \uc2  dollars. \par \par \uc2  Fears of higher U.S. interest rates in North American \par \par \uc2  markets subsided \par \par \uc2  after the Federal Reserve's latest Beige Book business survey \par \par \uc2  showed the U.S. \par \par \uc2  economy is strong but not overheating. \par \par \uc2      "There was initial concern in the money market regarding a \par \par \uc2  potential rate \par \par \uc2  hike... watching the Bank of Canada going in the 9.00 a.m. \par \par \uc2  period," said Reid \par \par \uc2  Farrill, executive director, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at CIBC Wood Gundy \par \par \uc2  Securities. \par \par \uc2  "Now that it doesn't appear that the bank is going to do \par \par \uc2  anything, we'll see if \par \par \uc2  we're going to test the C$1.4010/15 area." \par \par \uc2      If the Canadian dollar breaks through C$1.4415 (US$0.6937), \par \par \uc2  it could weaken \par \par \uc2  substantially, Farrill said. \par \par \uc2      But he added he did not expect \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell \par \par \uc2  U.S. dollars until it reaches around C$1.4460 (US$0.6916). \par \par \uc2      "There's some corporate interest to buy Canada, especially \par \par \uc2  at C$1.4410, \par \par \uc2  we've got fairly decent broadly-based interest by exporters to \par \par \uc2  buy Canada," one \par \par \uc2  dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "There was some nervousness this morning about a possible \par \par \uc2  rate hike (in \par \par \uc2  Canada), but I think that's a little bit premature right now. \par \par \uc2  We'd have to wait \par \par \uc2  for more data, a few more hints before they do that," the dealer \par \par \uc2  said. \par \par \uc2  The market will continue to seek any hints of the next \par \par \uc2  action by the U.S. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed at retaining sustained, non-inflationary \par \par \uc2  growth. \par \par \uc2  The market is awaiting the next key inflation indicator - \par \par \uc2  U.S. April jobs \par \par \uc2  data due out Friday. Economists polled by Reuters on average \par \par \uc2  forecast U.S. \par \par \uc2  employment growth at 259,000 after a surprise drop of 36,000 in \par \par \uc2  March, and the \par \par \uc2  jobless rate to be unchanged at 4.7 percent. \par \par \uc2  They said growth well above 300,000 should boost \par \par \uc2  expectations of a Fed \par \par \uc2  tightening. \par \par \uc2  Next week, the Bank of Canada will release its semi-annual \par \par \uc2  monetary policy \par \par \uc2  report. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses, the Canadian dollar, after crawling up \par \par \uc2  earlier, fell to \par \par \uc2  1.2251 marks from 1.2276 marks at the previous close here, and \par \par \uc2  was still quoted \par \par \uc2  a bit higher at 92.43 yen from 91.30 yen. \par \par \uc2      ((Masaru Sato, Reuters Toronto newsroom (416) 941-8107, \par \par \uc2  toronto.newsroom@reuters.com)) \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du5605w95\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
