\par\par \b \uc2  Canada dollar opens little changed. \b0\par\par\uc2 594 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Mai 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par FORECAST RANGE   1.4370/1.4420\tab \tab ASIAN CLOSE   1.4397\par RESISTANCE   1.4270  SUPPORT 1.4450\tab  HI 1.4410  LO 1.4378\par CANADA OPEN  1.4383  HI 1.4410\tab \tab EUROPE OPEN   1.4388\par PREV CLOSE   1.4390  LO 1.4380\tab \tab HI 1.4408  LO 1.4373\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ---------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  WEDNESDAY, MAY 6 \par \par \uc2  TREND: NEUTRAL. ACTIVITY: ACTIVE \par \par \uc2  *Canada dollar opened little changed at C$1.4383 (US$0.6953). \par \par \uc2  *Expectations of a BOC rate increase helped prop CAD this \par \par \uc2  morning, but no signs of BOC stepping in to stem CAD's fall at \par \par \uc2  this level. *Market awaiting US April jobs data Friday for \par \par \uc2  further hint of US inflation trend, thus Fed policy. \par \par \uc2  TORONTO, May 6 (Reuters) - The Canadian dollar opened \par \par \uc2  little changed at C$1.4383 (US$0.6953) on Wednesday in fairly \par \par \uc2  active trade. \par \par \uc2  Speculation that the Bank of Canada would raise a key \par \par \uc2  lending rate to stem the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fall helped prop it up in \par \par \uc2  early trade. \par \par \uc2  But there was no sign of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepping in this \par \par \uc2  morning, either raising rates or selling U.S. dollars for \par \par \uc2  Canada. \par \par \uc2  North American markets in general remained jittery over the \par \par \uc2  prospect of higher German and U.S. interest rates. Higher U.S. \par \par \uc2  rates, in theory, could favor the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the \par \par \uc2  low-yielding Canadian unit. \par \par \uc2  "There was initial concern in the money market regarding a \par \par \uc2  potential rate hike... watching the Bank of Canada going in the \par \par \uc2  9.00 a.m. period," said Reid Farrill, executive director, \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at CIBC Wood Gundy Securities. \par \par \uc2  He noted Canadian dollar buying brought the U.S. dollar \par \par \uc2  from C$1.4410 (US$0.6940) to C$1.4375/80 (US$0.6957/54) \par \par \uc2  earlier. \par \par \uc2  "Now that it doesn't appear that the bank is going to do \par \par \uc2  anything, see if we're going to test the C$1.4010/15 area," he \par \par \uc2  said. \par \par \uc2  If the Canadian dollar breaks through C$1.4415 (US$0.6937), \par \par \uc2  it could weaken substantially, Farrill said. \par \par \uc2  But he added that he did not expect \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to sell U.S. dollars until \par \par \uc2  it reaches around C$1.4460 (US$0.6916). \par \par \uc2  "There's lots of interest to sell (U.S.) dollars," said one \par \par \uc2  dealer. "Some corporate interest to buy Canada, especially at \par \par \uc2  C$1.4410, we've got fairly decent broad-based interest by \par \par \uc2  exporters to buy Canada." \par \par \uc2  "There was some nervousness this morning about a possible \par \par \uc2  rate hike (in Canada), but I think that's a little bit \par \par \uc2  premature right now. We'd have to wait for more data, a few \par \par \uc2  more hints before they do that," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The market will continue to seek any hints about the next \par \par \uc2  moves by the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed at retaining sustained, \par \par \uc2  non-inflationary growth. \par \par \uc2  The market is awaiting U.S. April jobs data due out Friday. \par \par \uc2  Economists polled by Reuters on average forecast U.S. \par \par \uc2  employment growth at 259.000 after a surprise drop of 36,000 in \par \par \uc2  March, and the jobless rate unchanged at 4.7 percent. \par \par \uc2  They said growth well above 300,000 should boost \par \par \uc2  expectations of a Fed tightening. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses, the Canadian dollar edged up to 1.2296 \par \par \uc2  marks from 1.2276 marks at the previous close here, and to \par \par \uc2  92.42 yen from 91.30 yen. \par \par \uc2  The yen remained weak on falling Japanese stocks and \par \par \uc2  concern over a slow pace of fixing its credit crunch. \par \par \uc2  ((Masaru Sato, Reuters Toronto newsroom (416) 941-8107, \par \par \uc2  toronto.newsroom@reuters.com)) \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du5605v7b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
