\par\par \b \uc2  =Canada  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2 /Policy -2: May Want Tighter Money \b0\par\par\uc2 351 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par 20:42\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    But the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's decision not to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and\par slow down the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's rise this month sent the reverse\par signal, Goldman's Kasumovich said.\par    The bank's inaction suggests it still wants to see\par monetary conditions tightened - its stated policy stance\par since last May - and it would prefer that tightening\par to come through appreciation in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rather than\par higher interest rates, Kasumovich said.\par    "I think it's consistent with the view that over a\par longer time horizon they would like to see tighter\par conditions, and they would perhaps like to see it through\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," he said. "At the same time, they have\par brought forward so much of the tightening they had planned\par to do though '98, even if the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were to stall, we\par probably wouldn't see a rate hike until the latter part of\par the year."\par    Kasumovich and others point to something else that\par might be keeping the bank out of action when its normal\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  point comes up - an \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the bank\par on Jan.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  9 that choked off an incipient rally sparked by\par strong employment numbers.\par    That \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  drew criticism from some \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par market players, who couldn't understand why the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would block an upswing when the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weakness\par had clearly been a concern to bank officials.\par    Andrew Pyle, chief strategist with ABN AMRO Hoare\par Govett, said the Jan. 9 \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  implied the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had a base level for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    "The market . . . took that as a signal and started to\par sell the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  aggressively," Pyle said. The Bank of\par Canada wants to avoid a repeat of that scenario, and\par that's one reason bank officials are not responding to\par recent gains by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the usual fashion.\par    "And I think that's quite natural - and I think it's\par probably very appropriate policy too."\par    Another factor dissuading the bank from sticking too\par strictly to its "normal" \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy is a reduced\par need to build \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves, Pyle suggested.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires  03-30-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1342EST\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du3u00ubm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
