\par\par \b \uc2  Canada Morning: C$ Still Heads Lower; Technically Negative \b0\par\par\uc2 334 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par 16:43\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Canadian dollar is still heading lower early Monday, continuing the trend begun late Thursday after the announcement of Jean Charest a bid for the leadership of the Quebec Liberal Party. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar traded at C$1.4225 at 9:39 a.m. EST (1439 GMT), from C$1.4210 at 8:00 a.m. EST (1300 GMT) and from C$1.4171 late Friday. \par \par \uc2  'There's nothing much to it - technically it was not a good close on Friday, then nothing happened in Asia or London, and now North American players are selling Canada again,' said a dealer with one of the major Canadian banks. \par \par \uc2  Canada's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been trading off the political plans of Charest for much of March, gaining ground on hopes the popular leader of the federal Conservative Party would jump into Quebec politics and challenge the separatist Parti Quebecois in an upcoming election. \par \par \uc2  Final confirmation of the move after the close on Thursday set up losses on Friday and again this session, as players took profits and a slightly bearish technical profile set in, said dealers. \par \par \uc2  Technically, the market now has its eye on C$1.4242, last week's spot U.S. dollar high. However, the dealer points out that at that level, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  just might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , capping any further U.S. dollar gains. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  tends to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  against intraday moves in either direction of 70 ticks or more (though it doesn't always). Friday's close was C$1.4172, putting the possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  zone somewhere just over C$1.4240. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par These are the exchange rates at 9:39 a.m. EST (1438 GMT), 8:00 a.m.\par EST (1300 GMT) and late Friday.\par    U.S./CDN    1.4225      1.4210       1.4171\par    CDN/DEM     1.2946      1.2909       1.2892\par    CDN/YEN     92.86       92.82        91.82\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 30-03-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1443GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1158 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du3u02oxw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
