\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada \highlight\uc2  Continued  \highlight22\uc2 Intervening \highlight\uc2  In Defense of Cdn Dlr \b0\par\par\uc2 265 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Januar 1998\par 18:01\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  continued its\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market in support of\par the Canadian dollar Friday, renewing its offer to sell the\par U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  around the C$1.4602.\par    It began \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  when the U.S. dollar hit C$1.4625\par following a morning increase in the bank rate. The rate was\par raised 1/2 point to 5.00%. The bank sold U.S. dollars\par repeatedly, coming every 5 ticks or so, said traders.\par    After the rate hike the Canadian dollar initially\par gapped higher, with the U.S. dollar moving from C$1.4667 to\par C$1.4595. It then reversed direction and slid back down,\par prompting the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    At 11:48 a.m. EST (1648 GMT), the U.S. dollar was\par trading at C$1.4560. It hit a low at C$1.4549.\par    Canada's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  came under selling pressure back in\par the fall at the first hints of a crisis in the Asian\par financial markets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  A sharp drop in commodity prices fueled\par the drop, because items such as lumber and major metals\par remain important elements to Canada's export economy.\par    A widening of the current-account deficit that to C$25.5\par billion in the third quarter of 1997, also contributed to\par the move lower, said dealers.\par    But many say the main sellers have been speculative type\par investors who've bet they can force rate hikes out of the\par Bank of Canada.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires  01-30-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1201EST\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  4346 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du1u00978\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
