\par\par \b \uc2  =Canada Rate Rise -2: Some Analysts Say Economy Resilient \b0\par\par\uc2 349 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Januar 1998\par 17:32\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Not all are gloomy. Warren Jestin, chief economist with the Bank of Nova Scotia, said, "You've got to remember, monetary policy is extremely geared for growth right now." A bank rate at 5% is still very attractive, he stressed. The rate hike should be enough to keep the U.S. dollar below C$1.4700, but if the Asian crisis flares up again, more rate increases will be needed. \par \par \uc2  "The idea that these sort of rates will somehow shut the economy down, I think, misses the very fundamental point that (they) are extraordinarily low to begin with," argued Jestin. \par \par \uc2  Through 1996, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  slashed interest rates to some of their lowest levels in decades in an attempt to recharge a moribund economy. \par \par \uc2  Others argue the rate increase was necessary to restore the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's credibility with international investors. "The (Canadian) dollar's weakness has overshot the downdraft in commodity prices," said Sherry Cooper, chief economist with Nesbitt Burns Inc., in a well-publicized pre-rate hike release. \par \par \uc2  The continued plunge in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a vivid sign that foreign investors were losing faith in the Bank of Canada, she said. \par \par \uc2  In the "near term, if commodity prices begin to look like they're improving a little bit and Asia begins to settle, this 50 basis points may do it," said Jestin. But he reckons another 50 basis points will be required later in the first half. \par \par \uc2  Since the rate increase, the U.S. dollar has fallen back to C$1.4588, but only after heavy selling by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Previous to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the U.S. dollar threatened to head back toward its all-time high at C$1.4684, hit Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Spence at Deutsche said if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is going to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  it should do so resolutely. It ought to raise rates enough to take control of the situation, but "with a view to unwinding the ease once the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has stabilized." \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires  01-30-98 \par \par \uc2  1132EST \par \par \uc2  4220 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du1u0095z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
