\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada \highlight\uc2  Seen  \highlight22\uc2 Intervening \highlight\uc2  In Defense of Cdn Dlr \b0\par\par\uc2 245 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Januar 1998\par 16:50\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market repeatedly Friday, selling U.S.\par dollars repeatedly in an effort to smooth out trading action\par after it increased the bank rate to bolster the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par said a trader in Toronto.\par    After the rate hike the Canadian dollar initially gapped\par higher, with the U.S. dollar moving from C$1.4667 to\par C$1.4595. It then reversed direction and slid back down,\par prompting the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    The trader said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  came roughly every five\par ticks starting when the U.S. dollar hit C$1.4625. It moved up\par to C$1.4642, but was trading at C$1.4620 at 10:43 a.m. EST\par (1543 GMT).\par    The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's unofficial policy is to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets after intraday moves in either direction of\par 70 ticks or more. It has been \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  more frequently\par than usual and at smaller swings in the Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par value in recent weeks as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  came under intense\par attack.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been under severe pressure in recent\par weeks from a variety of factors, including a current-account\par deficit that surged to C$25.5 billion in the third quarter of\par 1997, lower commodity prices stemming from the Asian\par financial crisis, and sustained negative yield spreads with\par the U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires  01-30-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1050EST\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  4346 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du1u0092a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
