\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Canada \highlight\uc2  Afternoon: C$ Up Sharply On Rate Hike,  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 340 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Januar 1998\par 22:38\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (Dow Jones)--It took a 1/2-point rate increase and aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but the Canadian dollar was pulled off all-time lows Friday. \par \par \uc2  Turning its back on news of a 0.3% drop in November gross domestic product, one many economists found disturbing, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  pushed the bank rate up to 5%. The move has fired up a vocal disagreement among market observers over its wisdom. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar traded at C$1.4542 at 4:13 p.m. EST (2113 GMT), down from C$1.4625 at 8:00 a.m. EST (1300 GMT) but down from C$1.4653 late Thursday. It hit an historic high Thursday at C$1.4684. \par \par \uc2  'Don't sacrifice the economy to save the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Mr. Thiessen,' wrote Tim O'Neill, chief economist with the Bank of Montreal, in an emphatic criticism of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strategy. \par \par \uc2  He sees little economic justification for higher interest rates because inflation is below target at 0.7%, unemployment is too high at 8.6%, the November data suggest economic momentum may be waning, and investors had not lost confidence in Canadian-dollar assets. \par \par \uc2  Previous to the rate increase, bonds had enjoyed an impressive bull run, widening yield spreads to U.S. Treasurys. \par \par \uc2  Many \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  players say they liked the move, but suggest its not enough. 'I like the idea of being long Canadian dollars now, but I don't love it,' said one big-bank trader on Bay Street. He praised the bank's decision to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  first at C$1.4625, and again at the lower C$1.4602. 'That sent a strong signal, lowering their \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  point,' he said. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts agreed: 'today the bank finally stepped up to the plate and did the correct thing,' said Andrew Pyle, chief strategist with ABN Amro Hoare Govett. Nesbitt Burns' chief economist, Sherry Cooper, also applauded the move. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 30-01-98 \par \par \uc2  2138GMT \par \par \uc2  1158 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du1u00t92\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
