\par\par \b \uc2  Canada Dlr Drops Below Recent Record Lows; USD Hit C$1.4597 \b0\par\par\uc2 277 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Januar 1998\par 23:14\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The U.S. dollar has broken through its record highs against the Canadian dollar, reaching C$1.4597, well above the previous record of C$1.4575 set on Friday. \par \par \uc2  That is the highest U.S. dollar level ever traded in the Canadian dollar's 140-year history. It occurs despite repeated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed at slowing the U.S. rise. \par \par \uc2  It settled back to C$1.4588 by 5:05 p.m. EST (2205 GMT). \par \par \uc2  Early trading actually saw the U.S. dollar down to C$1.4462, but morning news of a 1% increase in fourth-quarter U.S. employment costs reignited fear of a U.S. rate increase, and put the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  back on the upward track. (see 1158 for the Canadian dollar comment) \par \par \uc2  The Canadian dollar also suffers amid concern that the Bank of Canada is unwilling to raise rates in its defense. In outings last week, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials made clear they were concerned about the impact of the Asian crisis and a massive ice storm in Ontario and Quebec on the domestic economy. They implied a comfort with the weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the level of monetary conditions in the economy. \par \par \uc2  Indeed, many analysts say another significant increase in interest rates threatens to derail a fragile consumer-led economic recovery at a time when inflation is a mere 0.7%. If the bank raises rates too much, choking off growth, it could drive inflation even lower and eventually have to cut interest rates. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 27-01-98 \par \par \uc2  2214GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du1r00r3i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
