\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada Intervenes \highlight\uc2  -2: Sales Decline Spurs C$ Drop \b0\par\par\uc2 310 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Januar 1998\par 15:33\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Friday to sell U.S. dollars at C$1.4570 at around 8:55 a.m. EST (1355 GMT), said a trader in Toronto. \par \par \uc2  The Canadian dollar, which slipped well below its previous official all-time low Thursday, dropped rapidly this morning after news that Canadian retail sales dropped 1.2% in November from the previous month, well below economists' forecast of a 0.6% increase. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar closed at C$1.4533 Thursday. It was at C$1.4517 shortly before the release of the data at 8:30 a.m. EST (1300 GMT), plunged to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level of C$1.4569 by about 8:56 a.m. and is now at C$1.4533. \par \par \uc2  The drop in retail sales reinforces the market perception that the Bank of Canada will be reluctant to raise rates in defense of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  because of uncertainty about the health of the Canadian economy. \par \par \uc2  The consumer price index grew by only 0.7% in November, which is below the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target range of 1% to 3%. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's unofficial policy is to stand against intraday moves in either direction of 70 ticks or more in order to contain trading volatility. It has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  much more frequently in recent weeks - and after smaller moves in value - as the Canadian dollar tumbled to its all-time low. \par \par \uc2  Concerns about the impact of the financial troubles in Asian on commodity prices and Canadian exports, and a dramatic widening of the country's current-account deficit conspired to unsettle the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  late last year, and it has remained under serious pressure in the last few sessions. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires  01-23-98 \par \par \uc2  0933EST \par \par \uc2  4346 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du1n007ts\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
