\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada Intervenes \highlight\uc2  -2: Rate Increase Seen Unlikely \b0\par\par\uc2 302 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Januar 1998\par 17:02\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for a\par second time in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Thursday to sell\par U.S. dollars at C$1.4490-95 around 10:40 a.m. EST (1540\par GMT), said a trader in Toronto.\par    The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  occurred after the U.S. dollar broke\par through an historic high of C$1.4465 at 12:38 a.m. EST (0538\par GMT). The first round was at C$1.4480-85. It closed at\par C$1.4438 on Wednesday.\par    The U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  traded at C$1.4488 at 10:54 a.m. EST.\par    The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  usually \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  when the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par moves 70 ticks or more in either direction from the previous\par day's close.\par    But it has been \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  early, and more frequently\par in the last several weeks as the Canadian dollar succumbs to\par a variety of pressures. The economic and financial crisis in\par Asia has knocked commodity prices sharply lower, still an\par important element in Canadian exports; Canadian interest\par rates remain well below their U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  counterparts; and there\par was a sharp widening of the country's current-account\par deficit in third quarter. It hit an annualized rate of\par C$25.5 billion, or about 3% of gross domestic product.\par    Adding to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's woes, a speech by Bank of\par Canada Governor Gordon Thiessen on Tuesday was interpreted\par by market players as suggesting the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will not be\par raising interest rates anytime soon.\par    News this morning that the Canadian consumer price index\par increased only 0.7% in December - below the bank's target\par inflation range of 1% to 3% - is seen as further evidence\par that an interest rate hike is unlikely in the near term.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires  01-22-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1102EST\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  4346 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du1m006n3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
