\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada Intervenes \highlight\uc2  -2: Rate Increase Seen Unlikely \b0\par\par\uc2 292 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Januar 1998\par 14:47\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Thursday to sell U.S. dollars at C$1.4480-85 around 8:05 a.m. EST (1305 GMT), said a trader in Toronto. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is the first by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the U.S. dollar reached its all-time official high of C$1.4467 at 12:38 a.m. EST (0538 GMT). It closed at C$1.4438 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is now trading at C$1.4465. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  usually \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves 70 ticks or more in either direction from the previous day's close. It has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  more frequently in the last several weeks as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dropped rapidly in response to a variety of negative pressures, including the economic and financial crisis in Asia, negative yield spreads against the U.S., and a dramatic widening of the country's current-account deficit, which hit an annualized rate of C$25.5 billion in the third quarter of 1997. \par \par \uc2  Although it rallied for a few sessions at the end of 1997 and the beginning of this year, the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  came under intense pressure again this week after a speech by Bank of Canada Governor Gordon Thiessen on Tuesday was interpreted by market players as suggesting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not be raising interest rates. \par \par \uc2  News this morning that the Canadian consumer price index increased only 0.7% in December - below the bank's target inflation range of 1% to 3% - is seen as further evidence that an interest rate hike is unlikely in the near term. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires  01-22-98 \par \par \uc2  0847EST \par \par \uc2  4346 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du1m006gu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
