\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada Intervenes \highlight\uc2  -2: U.S. Dlr Nears All-Time High \b0\par\par\uc2 319 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Januar 1998\par 20:47\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Wednesday to sell U.S. dollars around C$1.4450 at 2:28 p.m. EST (1928 GMT), said a trader with a major bank in Toronto. \par \par \uc2  The move comes as the U.S. dollar creeps up on the Bank of Canada's recorded all-time high for the U.S. dollar at C$1.4465, touched Feb. 4, 1986. Some traders say the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  actually hit C$1.4480 in that session, but it is not recorded. \par \par \uc2  Normally, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would only enter the market after the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had moved about 70 ticks or more in either direction. However, the policy is unofficial and it has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  early repeatedly in the past two months as global financial market turmoil takes its toll on the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Market observers say falling commodity prices due to the expected economic slowdown in the Asian economies, and worries about Canada's trade performance in that environment, are the chief forces behind the Canadian dollar's weakness. \par \par \uc2  Earlier Wednesday, Statistics Canada said the November trade surplus actually widened to C$1.03 billion, confounding expectations it would narrow further from the revised C$432 million surplus in October. Exports rose 1.5%, clearly outpacing a 0.9% decline in imports. \par \par \uc2  And analysts say the data calm some fears the trade balance could fall into a deficit for the first time since 1976. \par \par \uc2  But the trade account still points to a deepening of the country's current-account deficit, which hit some 3% of gross domestic product in the third quarter. That spells trouble for the Canadian dollar. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar has moved back to C$1.4450 at 2:39 p.m. EST (1939 GMT). \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires  01-21-98 \par \par \uc2  1447EST \par \par \uc2  4346 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du1l005yk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
