\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada Intervenes \highlight\uc2  -2: U.S. Dlr Now At C$1.4402 \b0\par\par\uc2 262 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Januar 1998\par 15:36\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Tuesday to sell U.S. dollars between C$1.4410 and C$1.4415 at about 9:10 a.m. EST (1410 GMT), said a trader with a major bank in Toronto. \par \par \uc2  The move comes as the U.S. dollar threatens to break through December highs at C$1.4416, which would put it into levels not seen in just under 12 years and leave it targeted at C$1.4465, the all-time high set in Feb. 1986. \par \par \uc2  Normally, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would only enter the market after the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had moved about 70 ticks or more in either direction. However, the policy is unofficial and it has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  early repeatedly in the past two months as global financial market turmoil took its toll on the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Market observers say falling commodity prices due to the expected economic slowdown in the Asian economies, and worries about Canada's trade performance in that environment, are the chief forces behind the Canadian dollar's weakness. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, Statistics Canada releases November trade data amid concern that the trade balance may have fallen into a deficit for the first time since 1976. Exports have been lagging imports in a domestic economy charged up by low interest rates. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar has moved back to C$1.4402 at 9:28 a.m. EST (1428 GMT). \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires  01-20-98 \par \par