\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada Intervention \highlight\uc2  -2: Action Taken Early \b0\par\par\uc2 288 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Januar 1998\par 19:35\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets Thursday afternoon, selling U.S. dollars at\par C$1.4375 just before 1 p.m. EST (1800 GMT), according to\par traders.\par    The U.S. dollar was at C$1.4362 at 1:16 p.m. (1816 GMT).\par    The Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had been weakening off throughout\par the session, with the U.S. dollar climbing about 50 ticks\par over Wednesday's close of C$1.4327.\par    The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  came early by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's normal\par standards, as it usually \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  when the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  moves\par 70 ticks in either direction from the previous day's close.\par    The U.S. dollar had been edging closer to the 12-year\par high of C$1.4416 set on Dec. 29 on Thursday after trading in\par a fairly narrow range in the last few sessions. The U.S.\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's all-time high against the Canadian dollar was\par C$1.4465 set on Feb. 4, 1986.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    The Canadian dollar weakened off through late 1997,\par succumbing to a variety of negative factors including normal\par year-end pressures, uncertainty about the impact of Asian\par financial turmoil on commodity prices and Canadian exports,\par and a current-account deficit that surged to C$25.5 billion\par at annualized rates in the third quarter.\par    After touching bottom on Dec. 29, the Canadian dollar\par rebounded and enjoyed a rally that lasted into early 1998. It\par has weakened off in the last few sessions, and even news on\par Jan. 9 that the Canadian unemployment rate reached 8.6% - its\par lowest level since September 1990 - was not able to trigger\par sustained improvement in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires  01-15-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1335EST\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020020317du1f003vi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
