\par\par \b \uc2  Canada Afternoon: C$ Drops As Asia Refires Commodity Worry \b0\par\par\uc2 333 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Januar 1998\par 22:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (Dow Jones)--A resumption of the turmoil in the Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets had the Canadian dollar back under attack Tuesday, as it joined other commodity-linked \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in sharp losses. \par \par \uc2  Heavy selling earlier prompted repeated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and speculation is on once again that another rate hike may be required to shore up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was trading at C$1.4315 at 4:28 p.m. EST (2128 GMT), up from C$1.4293 at 8:00 a.m. EST (1300 GMT) and C$1.4232 late Monday. Traders say another test of C$1.4416 is possible, a level hit last week for the first time since Feb. 1986. \par \par \uc2  'I think the culprit is the renewed turmoil in Southeast Asia,' said Doug Porter, senior economist with Nesbitt Burns Inc. A bad day for the Indonesian rupiah and others in the region played on fears the crisis there is far from over and it could spark further losses in many commodity prices important to Canada's export-led economy. \par \par \uc2  The weakness in commidity prices 'is making the Canadian dollar less tolerant than it had been earlier to negative interest-rate differentials,' said Avery Shenfeld, senior economist with CIBC Wood Gundy Inc. A sharp discount in Canadian interest rates, relative to U.S. rates, has been blamed for months for the Canadian dollar's recent poor fortunes. \par \par \uc2  Indeed, this session the three-month treasury bill shot up 26 basis points to 4.18%, in fear that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness could eventually prompt the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to narrow that differential with another defensive rate increase. Even at 4.18% the treasury bill still yields 89 basis points less than the comparable U.S. bill. \par \par \uc2  On Dec. 12 the bank raised the key bank rate 1/2 point to 4.5%, citing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  losses to explain the move. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 06-01-98 \par \par \uc2  2130GMT \par \par \uc2  1158 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du16003jk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
