\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Canada \highlight\uc2  Morning: Cdn Dlr Weakens, Bk Of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada Intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 353 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Januar 1998\par 16:08\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Canadian dollar's New Year rally petered out Tuesday morning and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has plunged to levels that prompted the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets by selling U.S. dollars. \par \par \uc2  'I think the weakness we're seeing this morning is obviously related to renewed turmoil in Asia and obviously related to the divebombing we're seeing in oil right now,' said Andrew Pyle, economist with ABN AMRO Hoare Govett. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was trading at C$1.4308 at 10:00 a.m. EST (1500 GMT), up from C$1.4232 at 8:00 a.m. EST (1300 GMT) and C$1.4232 late Monday. \par \par \uc2  The Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had rallied in recent sessions after weakening dramatically in December. The U.S. dollar reached a 12-year high of C$1.4416 on Dec. 30 and then started to retrace its gains, moving down to levels last seen in mid-December. \par \par \uc2  Today is the first day the Canadian dollar rally has faltered. The U.S. dollar moved to C$1.4305 just before 9:00 a.m. EST (1400 GMT), prompting the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. The move was consistent with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets when the Canadian dollar moves 70 ticks or more from the previous day's close. \par \par \uc2  The bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in December, spending US $1.94 billion and reducing its reserves to US $17.97 billion. \par \par \uc2  Pyle said the renewed depreciation of the Indonesian rupiah - which has lost about 30% of its value since 1998 began - and other signs of instability in Asia are roiling global markets, and affecting the Canadian dollar. \par \par \uc2  The decline of crude oil prices is also a factor, he said. There has been widespread selling of crude oil and related product futures in the wake of expected return of Iraqi crude oil to the market and increased production by countries in the Organization of Petroluem Exporting zCountries. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 06-01-98 \par \par \uc2  1508GMT \par \par \uc2  1158 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du160039a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
