\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada Intervenes \highlight\uc2  -2: Third Round Tuesday \b0\par\par\uc2 275 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Januar 1998\par 19:17\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of Canada stepped into the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market for the third time Tuesday, selling\par U.S. dollars around C$1.4327 at 1:03 p.m. EST (1803 GMT),\par said a trader with a major bank in Toronto.\par    It first began \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Tuesday at C$1.4305 as the\par Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakened off significantly in morning\par trading. But that, and a second round, failed to stem the\par U.S. dollar's rise.\par    The U.S. dollar closed Monday at C$1.4237, and the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  typically \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market on intraday\par moves of more than 70 ticks in an effort to smooth trading\par action.\par    Throughout the month of December the BOC sold U.S.\par dollars repeatedly in defense of the Canadian as the\par troubles in the Asian markets, and an associated drop in key\par commodity prices, combined with a dramatic widening of the\par country's current-account deficit to unsettle the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    It spent just under US $2.0 billion in the process,\par according to figures released earlier Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    In the last week of 1997, the U.S. dollar retreated\par sharply from an almost 12-year high at C$1.4416, but many\par dealers were unconvinced the new levels could hold for long\par without more substantial demand.\par    Some technical analysts say there will be another test\par of that high, with the all-time U.S. dollar record at\par C$1.4465 the ultimate target.\par    The U.S. dollar traded at C$1.4323 at 1:07 p.m. EST\par (1807 GMT).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires  01-06-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1317EST\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  4346 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du160025a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
