\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada Intervenes \highlight\uc2  -2: Follows Earlier Actions \b0\par\par\uc2 268 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Januar 1998\par 17:35\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market for the second time Tuesday to\par sell U.S. dollars at C$1.4315 at around 11:00 a.m. EST\par (1600 GMT) in an effort to smooth out trading action, said\par a trader in Toronto.\par    It follows earlier \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  beginning at C$1.4305\par as the Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakened significantly in\par morning trading Tuesday. The U.S. dollar has been moving up\par from the Monday close at C$1.4237, forcing the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market in accordance with its\par unofficial policy of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  when the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  moves in\par either direction 70 ticks or more.\par    Throughout the month of December the BOC \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par repeatedly in the Canadian dollar's defense as the troubles\par in the Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets and a dramatic widening of\par the country's current-account deficit conspired to unsettle\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    It spent just under US$2.0 billion in the process,\par according to figures released earlier Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    In the last week of 1997, the U.S. dollar retreated\par sharply from an almost 12-year high at C$1.4416, but many\par dealers remain unconvinced that the new levels can hold for\par long without more substantial demand.\par    Some technical analysts say there will be another test\par of that high, with the all-time U.S. dollar record at\par C$1.4465 the ultimate target.\par    The U.S. dollar traded at C$1.4307 at 11:24 a.m. EST\par (1624 GMT).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires  01-06-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1135EST\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  4346 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du16001yl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
