\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada Intervenes \highlight\uc2  -2: C$ Remains Under Pressure \b0\par\par\uc2 241 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Dezember 1997\par 20:00\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Monday to sell U.S. dollars at\par C$1.4395 at around 1:20 p.m. EST (1820 GMT), said traders.\par    The Canadian dollar has been under heavy downward\par pressure in the past few weeks due to a series of factors,\par prompting frequent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    The U.S. dollar was trading at C$1.4368 at 8:00 a.m. and\par rose gradually through the morning until reaching the\par C$1.4395 that triggered the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's reported\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    The bank normally \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  when the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  moves 70\par ticks in either direction from the previous day's close to\par contain volatility, but it has been \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  more often\par during the recent period of intense pressure against the\par Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    Canada's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is suffering from a combination of\par uncertainty about the economic impact from the Asian\par financial crisis, the usual thin year-end demand conditions,\par negative yield spreads to the U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  and a current-account\par deficit at C$25.5 billion in the third quarter.\par    The bank also \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  several times last week as the\par Canadian dollar continued to edge downward in thin trading.\par    Some market sources were calling for repeated\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if the U.S. dollar rises again to C$1.4395 or\par above.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires  12-29-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1400EST\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  4346 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011006dtct02s75\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
