\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Canada \highlight\uc2  dollar closes firmer, aided by  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 183 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Dezember 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TORONTO, Dec 24 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar ended a short pre-holiday session slightly stronger on Wednesday, backing away from the C$1.4395 (US$0.6947) level as Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  took effect in light trading. \par \par \uc2  The unit quickly weakened to the C$1.4395 area after opening around C$1.4378 (US$0.6955) level, prompting Canada \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying and U.S. dollar selling by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Price movements are really being exaggerated," said Harvinder Kalirai, I.D.E.A. analyst. \par \par \uc2  The dollar finished at C$1.4340 (US$0.6974) after closing at C$1.4380 (US$0.6954) on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Canadian markets will shut down for Christmas and Boxing Day, re-opening on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said they see more weakness and very light flows in the week of New Year's. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses, the dollar rose to 1.2341 marks from 1.2332 marks at Tuesday's close and to 90.42 yen from 89.90 yen. \par \par \uc2  ((Lydia Zajc, Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8109)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtco00oh4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
