\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of Canada Sells -2: Thin Conditions Exacerbate Moves \b0\par\par\uc2 292 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Dezember 1997\par 15:01\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Wednesday morning to sell U.S.\par dollars in the C$1.4390-95 area at around 8:41 a.m. EST\par (1341 GMT), said a dealer.\par    He said the market is extremely thin with most players\par eager only to square up positions ahead of the Christmas\par holiday. "But if Chicago plays than there is no one here to\par stand against it," he added, noting that the modest amount\par of selling this morning originated on the International\par Monetary Market (IMM) in Chicago.\par    The Canadian dollar has been under heavy downward\par pressure in the past few weeks due to a series of factors,\par prompting frequent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The\par U.S. dollar trades less than a cent below its all-time high\par at C$1.4465 hit in Feb. 4, 1986, and many traders think it\par might breach that point soon.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Canada's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  suffers a combination of uncertainty\par about the economic impact from the Asian financial crisis,\par the usual thin yearend demand conditions, negative yield\par spreads to the U.S. and a current-account deficit at C$25.5\par billion in the third quarter.\par    The bank also \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  early in Monday's session,\par again on Tuesday, and several times last week. The U.S.\par dollar has moved back to C$1.4370 since the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par It closed Monday at C$1.4345.\par    Since \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  the U.S. dollar has moved back to\par trade around C$1.4386 (at 8:54 a.m. EST), but the dealer\par said a move over C$1.4400 this session can't be ruled out.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires  12-24-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0901EST\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  4346 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011006dtco02qju\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
