\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada Intervenes \highlight\uc2  -2: C$ Remains Under Pressure \b0\par\par\uc2 186 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Dezember 1997\par 22:36\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Tuesday to sell U.S. dollars at\par C$1.4375 at around 3:50 p.m. EST (2050 GMT), said traders.\par    The Canadian dollar has been under heavy downward\par pressure in the past few weeks due to a series of factors,\par prompting frequent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    It has continued to drift downward this week despite\par thinly staffed trading desks and dwindling volumes of\par trading activity in light of the rapidly approaching\par Christmas holiday.\par    Canada's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  suffers a combination of uncertainty\par about the economic impact from the Asian financial crisis,\par the usual thin year-end demand conditions, negative yield\par spreads to the U.S. and a current-account deficit at C$25.5\par billion in the third quarter.\par    The bank also \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  early in Monday's session, and\par several times last week. The U.S. dollar has moved back to\par C$1.4370 since the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . It closed Monday at\par C$1.4345.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires  12-23-97 \par \par \uc2  1636EST \par \par \uc2  4346 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011006dtcn02pw6\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph